s the shared baseline row, exactly as in the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/31f7f899/D7/2/code.py:53:# - Source bars all cross the shared baseline row; right-half output bars use the same vertical\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/7b3084d4/D2/3/code.py:273:    if FEATURE == \"cross5\":\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/7b3084d4/D2/3/code.py:413:    if FEATURE == \"cross5\":\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/da515329/D1/1/code.py:27:#     - Same as the seed task: one hollow teal plus-sign cross on black.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/da515329/D1/1/code.py:55:#     - Center detection by row/column argmax remains valid because the input cross is\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/da515329/D1/1/code.py:212:    Grow four spiral wall paths from the tips of a teal cross, with launch direction tied to tip orientation.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/da515329/D1/1/code.py:215:    - bg = 0 (black). A single teal (8) cross has a one-cell empty hole at its center.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/332f06d7/D5/1/code.py:20:#     - Colors stay semantically stable across examples:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/7b3084d4/D2/2/code.py:273:    if FEATURE == \"cross5\":\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/7b3084d4/D2/2/code.py:413:    if FEATURE == \"cross5\":\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/da515329/D1/2/code.py:17:# The input object stays the same: one hollow teal cross on black. The new behavior is\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/da515329/D1/2/code.py:26:# 3. Compute a visible square-ring index from the cross center and arm length, and pick\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/da515329/D1/2/code.py:59:def _find_cross(grid: np.ndarray) -> tuple[int, int, int]:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/da515329/D1/2/code.py:238:    Build an alternating-handed rectangular spiral from a teal cross.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/da515329/D1/2/code.py:241:    - bg = 0 (black). One teal (8) cross with equal arms and a one-cell center hole.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/cesh