3e/D1/1/code.py:33:- Cap colors are drawn from a tiny 2-color palette reused across buckets; fill colors are\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/97d7923e/D1/1/code.py:64:- Because the same cap colors repeat across several buckets, any attempt to solve by color\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/97d7923e/D1/1/code.py:175:      Cap colors may repeat across different buckets and are not the grouping key.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/db695cfb/D6/2/code.py:54:#    - Across examples, the visible relation \"line goes away from the two blue legs\" is stable.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/db695cfb/D6/2/code.py:60:#    - Paths and rays are separated across different objects to avoid cluttered ambiguity.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/2ba387bc/D9/0/code.py:60:- Every sample has at least one cross-type shared color: some frame color also appears on some solid.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/2ba387bc/D9/0/code.py:78:- The key metric is `shared_cross_type_colors = |frame_colors ∩ solid_colors|`.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/2ba387bc/D9/0/code.py:135:    - Colors are no longer unique across objects.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/2ba387bc/D9/0/code.py:174:        \"shared_cross_type_colors\": int(len(shared)),\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/2ba387bc/D9/0/code.py:229:    if info[\"shared_cross_type_colors\"] < 1:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/332f06d7/D16/1/code.py:61:#    - Across examples, the moving square's color changes, so humans cannot rely on \"black moves\".\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/5961cc34/D12/2/code.py:19:#    This variant replaces it with a central cross marker: one yellow center pixel\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/5961cc34/D12/2/code.py:24:#    New flow: center cross -> four simultaneous thin rays (up/down/left/right) ->\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/5961cc34/D12/2/code.py:41:#    The generator reserves the central cross, keeps blobs separated by a 1-pixel\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/5961cc34/D12/2/code.p